{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan review 2026-10-18 returned BLOCK on one move: S4 specified \"reaps the process group\" without naming the existing shared helper, so a reviewer could not tell whether a second reaper would be written. Description updated: S4 and AC3 now name `rebar._proc.reap_process_group` (`src/rebar/_proc.py:38`, already the reaper for `grounding/harness.py`, `acli_subprocess.py`, and `wiki_render.py`) as the only reaper, and AC3 states the in-session checks: a monkeypatch test on the `_bridge_runner` import site, a real child-plus-grandchild timeout test asserting both pids are gone, and a grep proving no `os.kill`/`killpg`/`SIG*` call site was added outside `_proc.py`. The epic's 15 advisory findings (criterion-6 ownership propagation to children, lease-failure disposition example) are left for the story authors; none blocks."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792363374040837964,"uuid":"c64255c7-3859-41a8-8d1e-f2d4528c7554"}